   "html_text": "The general aim of classical AI had been all but quietly given up after the AI winters, though a small group pushed for the idea that classical AI should focus directly on “Artificial General Intelligence” (AGI) – organising a niche conference series under that title since 2008. In the last 10 years, it has become common to ask once again, whether we might be on a road to a general AI, now understood to be based mainly on ML. The old label “AGI” is now often used to differentiate the aim of gene",
